            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`call-interactively` passes exactly the arguments the `(interactive …)` descriptor names — none at all when there is no descriptor, one per newline-separated code letter when it is a string. A required parameter left unsupplied is a `wrong-number-of-arguments` signal at the first invocation, and nothing before that reports it."
              },
              "id": "elisp-interactive-arity-mismatch",
              "properties": {
                "category": "arity",
                "fixable": false,
                "rationale": "`call-interactively` passes exactly the arguments the `(interactive …)` descriptor names — none at all when there is no descriptor, one per newline-separated code letter when it is a string. A required parameter left unsupplied is a `wrong-number-of-arguments` signal at the first invocation, and nothing before that reports it.",
                "severity": "error",
                "tags": []
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "an interactive spec that supplies fewer arguments than the lambda list requires"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`add-hook` compares with `equal`, so an anonymous function is deduplicated only while it is textually unchanged. Edit the lambda and re-evaluate the file and the hook holds both versions; `add-hook`'s own docstring recommends a function symbol for exactly this reason, and notes the comparison cost as a second one."
              },
              "id": "elisp-hook-lambda",
              "properties": {
                "category": "suspicious",
                "fixable": false,
                "rationale": "`add-hook` compares with `equal`, so an anonymous function is deduplicated only while it is textually unchanged. Edit the lambda and re-evaluate the file and the hook holds both versions; `add-hook`'s own docstring recommends a function symbol for exactly this reason, and notes the comparison cost as a second one.",
                "severity": "warning",
                "tags": [
                  "pedantic",
                  "style"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "a lambda on a hook, which re-evaluating the file adds a second copy of"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`save-excursion` saves point in whichever buffer is current when it runs, so wrapping a `set-buffer` saves point in the buffer being left rather than the one being worked in. The current buffer *is* restored — that part has not changed — but the point protection the form appears to ask for is not the one it provides. Emacs's own byte compiler emits `Use 'with-current-buffer' rather than save-excursion+set-buffer` for this exact pair."
              },
              "id": "elisp-save-excursion-set-buffer",
              "properties": {
                "category": "suspicious",
                "fixable": false,
                "rationale": "`save-excursion` saves point in whichever buffer is current when it runs, so wrapping a `set-buffer` saves point in the buffer being left rather than the one being worked in. The current buffer *is* restored — that part has not changed — but the point protection the form appears to ask for is not the one it provides. Emacs's own byte compiler emits `Use 'with-current-buffer' rather than save-excursion+set-buffer` for this exact pair.",
                "severity": "warning",
                "tags": []
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "save-excursion wrapping set-buffer, which saves point in the buffer it then leaves"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`cl.el` and `cl-compat.el` ship from `lisp/obsolete/` and announce themselves as deprecated on load. They exist only to define the unprefixed aliases that `cl-lib` replaced with `cl-`-prefixed names."
              },
